WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:01.760
The web is visual.

00:00:01.760 --> 00:00:04.700
Well, obviously,
otherwise this course wouldn't exist.

00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:08.670
But not all people surfing the web have
the ability to see images like this one.

00:00:08.670 --> 00:00:09.960
For the visually impaired,

00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:13.060
screen readers are essential
to make sense of the web.

00:00:13.060 --> 00:00:14.450
This is Lynx.

00:00:14.450 --> 00:00:18.050
It's an all text browser and
this is what Reddit looks like on Lynx.

00:00:18.050 --> 00:00:22.470
Without images, this is all a user
has to decipher your website and

00:00:22.470 --> 00:00:24.650
they usually won't even be reading it.

00:00:24.650 --> 00:00:27.590
They'll be hearing it through
a screen reader like ChromeVox.

00:00:27.590 --> 00:00:30.120
The good news is that you can
still make images meaningful

00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:32.890
by using alt attributes responsibly.

00:00:32.890 --> 00:00:34.948
Here, let me show you what I mean.

00:00:34.948 --> 00:00:36.160
I've enabled ChromeVox,

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:39.750
which is a screen reader that
will be reading this page to you.

00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:41.920
Here, let's see what it has to say.

00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:45.100
&gt;&gt; The internet thanks you for
being responsible with your alt tags.

00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:49.070
To replicate the experience of being
visually impaired, I'm giving you

00:00:49.070 --> 00:00:52.346
some information using images that
don't make any sense on their own,

00:00:52.346 --> 00:00:53.920
or at all, really.

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:56.320
Don't leave your visually impaired
visitors out in the cold.

00:00:56.320 --> 00:00:59.010
Here are some tips about alt tags.

00:00:59.010 --> 00:01:02.270
Alt tags should be descriptive for
important images,

00:01:02.270 --> 00:01:07.370
like this body surfer because body
surfing is important, I guess.

00:01:07.370 --> 00:01:08.820
Alt tags should be empty for

00:01:08.820 --> 00:01:12.680
images that are just decorations,
like this boiler image.

00:01:12.680 --> 00:01:14.080
Do you get the joke?

00:01:14.080 --> 00:01:16.700
It's a boiler to represent
boilerplate code,

00:01:16.700 --> 00:01:19.215
which is sometimes empty of content.

00:01:19.215 --> 00:01:23.100
Alt tags should be set on every image
just like this pig is set on being so

00:01:23.100 --> 00:01:23.740
darn cute.

00:01:24.770 --> 00:01:26.150
&gt;&gt; So there you have it.

00:01:26.150 --> 00:01:28.960
Check the instructor notes if you
want to see the tips that ChromeVox

00:01:28.960 --> 00:01:30.300
just read to you.

00:01:30.300 --> 00:01:33.770
Oh, and by the way, to get ChromeVox,
it's just a Chrome extension,

00:01:33.770 --> 00:01:35.240
so it's really easy to install.

